# Flask Template Rules

## Template Structure
- Extend base.html for all templates
- Use consistent block names
- Organize CSS/JS includes properly
- Follow responsive design principles

## Base Template
```html
{% extends 'base.html' %}

{% block title %}Page Title{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<div class="container">
    <!-- Page content here -->
</div>
{% endblock %}

{% block scripts %}
<!-- Page-specific scripts -->
{% endblock %}
```

## Styling Guidelines
- Use Bootstrap classes consistently
- Follow mobile-first approach
- Maintain color scheme variables
- Use proper spacing classes

## Component Organization
- Break down into reusable components
- Use macros for repeated elements
- Keep templates DRY
- Document complex components

## Form Handling
- Use WTForms for form generation
- Include CSRF protection
- Implement proper validation
- Show error messages clearly

## JavaScript Integration
- Load scripts at bottom of page
- Use async/defer where appropriate
- Implement proper error handling
- Follow event delegation patterns

## SEO Guidelines
- Include proper meta tags
- Use semantic HTML elements
- Implement structured data
- Optimize for accessibility

## Error Templates
- Create consistent error pages
- Include helpful error messages
- Provide navigation options
- Log error occurrences 

// Eviction Management System Flask Templates Rules
// These rules define the structure and conventions for Flask templates

// Directory Structure
/**
 * Templates should be organized in the following directory structure:
 * 
 * templates/
 * ├── base.html                  # Base template with common elements
 * ├── components/                # Reusable UI components
 * │   ├── alerts.html            # Alert and notification components
 * │   ├── forms.html             # Form field components and layouts
 * │   ├── modals.html            # Modal dialog components
 * │   ├── navigation.html        # Navigation components (navbar, sidebar)
 * │   ├── pagination.html        # Pagination controls
 * │   └── tables.html            # Table and data display components
 * ├── layouts/                   # Page layout templates
 * │   ├── dashboard.html         # Dashboard layout
 * │   ├── fullwidth.html         # Full-width page layout
 * │   └── sidebar.html           # Page with sidebar layout
 * ├── pages/                     # Specific page templates
 * │   ├── auth/                  # Authentication pages
 * │   │   ├── login.html
 * │   │   ├── register.html
 * │   │   └── reset_password.html
 * │   ├── dashboard/             # Dashboard pages
 * │   │   ├── index.html
 * │   │   ├── analytics.html
 * │   │   └── reports.html
 * │   ├── evictions/             # Eviction management pages
 * │   │   ├── details.html
 * │   │   ├── form.html
 * │   │   ├── list.html
 * │   │   └── timeline.html
 * │   ├── properties/            # Property management pages
 * │   │   ├── details.html
 * │   │   ├── form.html
 * │   │   └── list.html
 * │   └── tenants/               # Tenant management pages
 * │       ├── details.html
 * │       ├── form.html
 * │       └── list.html
 * ├── emails/                    # Email templates
 * │   ├── notification.html
 * │   ├── password_reset.html
 * │   └── welcome.html
 * └── errors/                    # Error page templates
 *     ├── 400.html
 *     ├── 403.html
 *     ├── 404.html
 *     └── 500.html
 */

// Base Template Structure
/**
 * Every base.html template should include:
 * - HTML5 doctype declaration
 * - Viewport meta tag for responsive design
 * - CSS and JavaScript includes in the appropriate locations
 * - Flash message handling
 * - Common navigation elements
 * - Footer with copyright and legal information
 * 
 * Example structure:
 * ```html
 * <!DOCTYPE html>
 * <html lang="en">
 * <head>
 *     <meta charset="UTF-8">
 *     <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
 *     <title>{% block title %}Eviction Management System{% endblock %}</title>
 *     <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ url_for('static', filename='css/main.css') }}">
 *     {% block extra_css %}{% endblock %}
 * </head>
 * <body class="{% block body_class %}{% endblock %}">
 *     <header>
 *         {% include 'components/navigation.html' %}
 *     </header>
 *     
 *     <main class="container my-4">
 *         {% include 'components/alerts.html' %}
 *         {% block content %}{% endblock %}
 *     </main>
 *     
 *     <footer class="footer mt-auto py-3 bg-light">
 *         <div class="container">
 *             <span class="text-muted">© 2025 Eviction Management System</span>
 *         </div>
 *     </footer>
 *     
 *     <script src="{{ url_for('static', filename='js/main.js') }}"></script>
 *     {% block extra_js %}{% endblock %}
 * </body>
 * </html>
 * ```
 */

// Component Guidelines
/**
 * Reusable components should:
 * - Accept template variables for customization
 * - Include default values where appropriate
 * - Be well-documented with comments
 * - Handle empty states gracefully
 * 
 * Example alert component:
 * ```html
 * {# components/alerts.html #}
 * {% macro alert(type='info', dismissible=true, message='') %}
 * <div class="alert alert-{{ type }} {% if dismissible %}alert-dismissible fade show{% endif %}" role="alert">
 *     {{ message }}
 *     {% if dismissible %}
 *     <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-bs-dismiss="alert" aria-label="Close"></button>
 *     {% endif %}
 * </div>
 * {% endmacro %}
 * 
 * {# Usage in another template #}
 * {% from 'components/alerts.html' import alert %}
 * {{ alert('danger', true, 'This action cannot be undone.') }}
 * ```
 */

// Form Handling
/**
 * Form templates should:
 * - Use proper HTML5 form elements and attributes
 * - Include CSRF protection
 * - Provide clear validation feedback
 * - Group related form elements together
 * - Use consistent styling
 * 
 * Example form component:
 * ```html
 * {# components/forms.html #}
 * {% macro form_field(field) %}
 * <div class="mb-3">
 *     {{ field.label(class="form-label") }}
 *     {{ field(class="form-control " + ("is-invalid" if field.errors else "")) }}
 *     {% if field.errors %}
 *     <div class="invalid-feedback">
 *         {% for error in field.errors %}
 *         <span>{{ error }}</span>
 *         {% endfor %}
 *     </div>
 *     {% endif %}
 *     {% if field.description %}
 *     <small class="form-text text-muted">{{ field.description }}</small>
 *     {% endif %}
 * </div>
 * {% endmacro %}
 * 
 * {# Usage in another template #}
 * {% from 'components/forms.html' import form_field %}
 * <form method="post">
 *     {{ form.csrf_token }}
 *     {{ form_field(form.name) }}
 *     {{ form_field(form.email) }}
 *     <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Submit</button>
 * </form>
 * ```
 */

// Data Display
/**
 * Data tables should:
 * - Include responsive design considerations
 * - Provide sorting options where appropriate
 * - Include pagination for large datasets
 * - Display clear empty states
 * - Include action buttons with consistent styling
 * 
 * Example table component:
 * ```html
 * {# components/tables.html #}
 * {% macro data_table(headers, data, actions=true) %}
 * <div class="table-responsive">
 *     <table class="table table-striped table-hover">
 *         <thead>
 *             <tr>
 *                 {% for header in headers %}
 *                 <th scope="col">{{ header }}</th>
 *                 {% endfor %}
 *                 {% if actions %}
 *                 <th scope="col">Actions</th>
 *                 {% endif %}
 *             </tr>
 *         </thead>
 *         <tbody>
 *             {% if data %}
 *             {% for row in data %}
 *             <tr>
 *                 {% for cell in row %}
 *                 <td>{{ cell }}</td>
 *                 {% endfor %}
 *                 {% if actions %}
 *                 <td>
 *                     <a href="{{ url_for('view_item', id=row.id) }}" class="btn btn-sm btn-info">View</a>
 *                     <a href="{{ url_for('edit_item', id=row.id) }}" class="btn btn-sm btn-primary">Edit</a>
 *                     <a href="{{ url_for('delete_item', id=row.id) }}" class="btn btn-sm btn-danger">Delete</a>
 *                 </td>
 *                 {% endif %}
 *             </tr>
 *             {% endfor %}
 *             {% else %}
 *             <tr>
 *                 <td colspan="{{ headers|length + (1 if actions else 0) }}" class="text-center">
 *                     No data available
 *                 </td>
 *             </tr>
 *             {% endif %}
 *         </tbody>
 *     </table>
 * </div>
 * {% endmacro %}
 * ```
 */

// Navigation
/**
 * Navigation components should:
 * - Highlight active navigation items
 * - Be responsive on all device sizes
 * - Include proper accessibility attributes
 * - Support both authenticated and unauthenticated states
 * 
 * Example navigation component:
 * ```html
 * {# components/navigation.html #}
 * <nav class="navbar navbar-expand-lg navbar-dark bg-primary">
 *     <div class="container-fluid">
 *         <a class="navbar-brand" href="{{ url_for('index') }}">
 *             <img src="{{ url_for('static', filename='img/logo.png') }}" alt="Logo" height="30">
 *             Eviction Management
 *         </a>
 *         <button class="navbar-toggler" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#navbarNav">
 *             <span class="navbar-toggler-icon"></span>
 *         </button>
 *         <div class="collapse navbar-collapse" id="navbarNav">
 *             <ul class="navbar-nav me-auto">
 *                 <li class="nav-item">
 *                     <a class="nav-link {{ 'active' if request.endpoint == 'dashboard' }}" href="{{ url_for('dashboard') }}">Dashboard</a>
 *                 </li>
 *                 <li class="nav-item">
 *                     <a class="nav-link {{ 'active' if 'evictions' in request.endpoint }}" href="{{ url_for('evictions.list') }}">Evictions</a>
 *                 </li>
 *                 <li class="nav-item">
 *                     <a class="nav-link {{ 'active' if 'properties' in request.endpoint }}" href="{{ url_for('properties.list') }}">Properties</a>
 *                 </li>
 *                 <li class="nav-item">
 *                     <a class="nav-link {{ 'active' if 'reports' in request.endpoint }}" href="{{ url_for('reports.list') }}">Reports</a>
 *                 </li>
 *             </ul>
 *             <ul class="navbar-nav">
 *                 {% if current_user.is_authenticated %}
 *                 <li class="nav-item dropdown">
 *                     <a class="nav-link dropdown-toggle" data-bs-toggle="dropdown" href="#" role="button">
 *                         {{ current_user.name }}
 *                     </a>
 *                     <ul class="dropdown-menu dropdown-menu-end">
 *                         <li><a class="dropdown-item" href="{{ url_for('profile') }}">Profile</a></li>
 *                         <li><a class="dropdown-item" href="{{ url_for('settings') }}">Settings</a></li>
 *                         <li><hr class="dropdown-divider"></li>
 *                         <li><a class="dropdown-item" href="{{ url_for('logout') }}">Logout</a></li>
 *                     </ul>
 *                 </li>
 *                 {% else %}
 *                 <li class="nav-item">
 *                     <a class="nav-link" href="{{ url_for('login') }}">Login</a>
 *                 </li>
 *                 <li class="nav-item">
 *                     <a class="nav-link" href="{{ url_for('register') }}">Register</a>
 *                 </li>
 *                 {% endif %}
 *             </ul>
 *         </div>
 *     </div>
 * </nav>
 * ```
 */

// Modals
/**
 * Modal components should:
 * - Be accessible with proper attributes
 * - Include header, body, and footer sections
 * - Support form submission when required
 * - Have clear action buttons
 * 
 * Example modal component:
 * ```html
 * {# components/modals.html #}
 * {% macro modal(id, title, content, footer='', size='') %}
 * <div class="modal fade" id="{{ id }}" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="{{ id }}Label" aria-hidden="true">
 *     <div class="modal-dialog {{ size }}">
 *         <div class="modal-content">
 *             <div class="modal-header">
 *                 <h5 class="modal-title" id="{{ id }}Label">{{ title }}</h5>
 *                 <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-bs-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Close"></button>
 *             </div>
 *             <div class="modal-body">
 *                 {{ content }}
 *             </div>
 *             {% if footer %}
 *             <div class="modal-footer">
 *                 {{ footer }}
 *             </div>
 *             {% endif %}
 *         </div>
 *     </div>
 * </div>
 * {% endmacro %}
 * 
 * {# Usage example #}
 * {% from 'components/modals.html' import modal %}
 * {% set content %}
 *     <p>Are you sure you want to delete this eviction record?</p>
 *     <p>This action cannot be undone.</p>
 * {% endset %}
 * {% set footer %}
 *     <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" data-bs-dismiss="modal">Cancel</button>
 *     <form method="post" action="{{ url_for('delete_eviction', id=eviction.id) }}" class="d-inline">
 *         <button type="submit" class="btn btn-danger">Delete</button>
 *     </form>
 * {% endset %}
 * {{ modal('delete-modal', 'Confirm Deletion', content, footer) }}
 * ```
 */

// Error Pages
/**
 * Error templates should:
 * - Provide clear error messages
 * - Offer helpful navigation options
 * - Maintain consistent branding
 * - Be responsive on all device sizes
 * 
 * Example 404 error page:
 * ```html
 * {# errors/404.html #}
 * {% extends 'base.html' %}
 * 
 * {% block title %}Page Not Found{% endblock %}
 * 
 * {% block content %}
 * <div class="text-center py-5">
 *     <h1 class="display-1">404</h1>
 *     <h2 class="mb-4">Page Not Found</h2>
 *     <p class="lead">The page you are looking for doesn't exist or has been moved.</p>
 *     <div class="mt-4">
 *         <a href="{{ url_for('index') }}" class="btn btn-primary">Go to Homepage</a>
 *         <a href="javascript:history.back()" class="btn btn-outline-secondary ms-2">Go Back</a>
 *     </div>
 * </div>
 * {% endblock %}
 * ```
 */

// Pagination
/**
 * Pagination components should:
 * - Be responsive on all device sizes
 * - Show current page and total pages
 * - Include previous and next buttons
 * - Handle first and last page edge cases
 * 
 * Example pagination component:
 * ```html
 * {# components/pagination.html #}
 * {% macro pagination(page, total_pages, endpoint, **kwargs) %}
 * <nav aria-label="Page navigation">
 *     <ul class="pagination justify-content-center">
 *         <li class="page-item {{ 'disabled' if page == 1 else '' }}">
 *             <a class="page-link" href="{{ url_for(endpoint, page=1, **kwargs) }}" aria-label="First">
 *                 <span aria-hidden="true">&laquo;&laquo;</span>
 *             </a>
 *         </li>
 *         <li class="page-item {{ 'disabled' if page == 1 else '' }}">
 *             <a class="page-link" href="{{ url_for(endpoint, page=page-1, **kwargs) }}" aria-label="Previous">
 *                 <span aria-hidden="true">&laquo;</span>
 *             </a>
 *         </li>
 *         
 *         {% for p in range(max(1, page-2), min(total_pages+1, page+3)) %}
 *         <li class="page-item {{ 'active' if p == page else '' }}">
 *             <a class="page-link" href="{{ url_for(endpoint, page=p, **kwargs) }}">{{ p }}</a>
 *         </li>
 *         {% endfor %}
 *         
 *         <li class="page-item {{ 'disabled' if page == total_pages else '' }}">
 *             <a class="page-link" href="{{ url_for(endpoint, page=page+1, **kwargs) }}" aria-label="Next">
 *                 <span aria-hidden="true">&raquo;</span>
 *             </a>
 *         </li>
 *         <li class="page-item {{ 'disabled' if page == total_pages else '' }}">
 *             <a class="page-link" href="{{ url_for(endpoint, page=total_pages, **kwargs) }}" aria-label="Last">
 *                 <span aria-hidden="true">&raquo;&raquo;</span>
 *             </a>
 *         </li>
 *     </ul>
 * </nav>
 * {% endmacro %}
 * ```
 */

// Timeline Display
/**
 * Eviction timeline components should:
 * - Show clear progression of steps
 * - Highlight current stage
 * - Include dates for each step
 * - Provide detailed information on hover/click
 * 
 * Example timeline component:
 * ```html
 * {# evictions/timeline.html #}
 * <div class="eviction-timeline">
 *     <div class="timeline-container">
 *         {% for step in timeline %}
 *         <div class="timeline-step {{ step.status }}">
 *             <div class="timeline-marker"></div>
 *             <div class="timeline-content">
 *                 <h4>{{ step.title }}</h4>
 *                 <p class="timeline-date">{{ step.date }}</p>
 *                 <div class="timeline-details">
 *                     {{ step.details }}
 *                 </div>
 *             </div>
 *         </div>
 *         {% endfor %}
 *     </div>
 * </div>
 * ```
 */

// Dashboard Components
/**
 * Dashboard components should:
 * - Present key metrics in a visually appealing way
 * - Use charts and graphs for data visualization
 * - Include filters for customizing data display
 * - Provide links to detailed views
 * 
 * Example dashboard component:
 * ```html
 * {# dashboard/index.html #}
 * <div class="row row-cols-1 row-cols-md-2 row-cols-xl-4 g-4 mb-4">
 *     <div class="col">
 *         <div class="card h-100">
 *             <div class="card-body">
 *                 <h5 class="card-title">Active Evictions</h5>
 *                 <p class="card-text fs-1">{{ stats.active_evictions }}</p>
 *                 <p class="card-text text-muted">
 *                     <span class="{{ 'text-success' if stats.active_evictions_change < 0 else 'text-danger' }}">
 *                         {{ stats.active_evictions_change }}%
 *                     </span>
 *                     from last month
 *                 </p>
 *             </div>
 *             <div class="card-footer">
 *                 <a href="{{ url_for('evictions.list', status='active') }}" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary">View All</a>
 *             </div>
 *         </div>
 *     </div>
 *     <!-- Additional metric cards here -->
 * </div>
 * 
 * <div class="row g-4">
 *     <div class="col-12 col-xl-8">
 *         <div class="card h-100">
 *             <div class="card-header d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center">
 *                 <h5 class="card-title mb-0">Eviction Trends</h5>
 *                 <div class="btn-group">
 *                     <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary period-selector" data-period="month">Month</button>
 *                     <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary period-selector" data-period="quarter">Quarter</button>
 *                     <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary period-selector active" data-period="year">Year</button>
 *                 </div>
 *             </div>
 *             <div class="card-body">
 *                 <canvas id="eviction-trends-chart"></canvas>
 *             </div>
 *         </div>
 *     </div>
 *     <div class="col-12 col-xl-4">
 *         <div class="card h-100">
 *             <div class="card-header">
 *                 <h5 class="card-title mb-0">Eviction Status Distribution</h5>
 *             </div>
 *             <div class="card-body">
 *                 <canvas id="eviction-status-chart"></canvas>
 *             </div>
 *         </div>
 *     </div>
 * </div>
 * ```
 */

// Email Templates
/**
 * Email templates should:
 * - Use a simple, accessible design
 * - Include both HTML and plain text versions
 * - Be responsive for mobile email clients
 * - Include clear calls to action
 * - Provide unsubscribe options when appropriate
 * 
 * Example email template:
 * ```html
 * {# emails/notification.html #}
 * <!DOCTYPE html>
 * <html>
 * <head>
 *     <meta charset="UTF-8">
 *     <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
 *     <title>{{ subject }}</title>
 * </head>
 * <body style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; line-height: 1.6; color: #333; max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px;">
 *     <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 20px;">
 *         <img src="{{ url_for('static', filename='img/logo-email.png', _external=True) }}" alt="Eviction Management System Logo" style="max-width: 200px;">
 *     </div>
 *     
 *     <div style="background-color: #f8f9fa; padding: 20px; border-radius: 5px;">
 *         <h1 style="color: #0d6efd; margin-top: 0;">{{ title }}</h1>
 *         
 *         {{ content }}
 *         
 *         {% if action_url and action_text %}
 *         <div style="text-align: center; margin: 30px 0;">
 *             <a href="{{ action_url }}" style="background-color: #0d6efd; color: white; padding: 10px 20px; text-decoration: none; border-radius: 5px; display: inline-block;">{{ action_text }}</a>
 *         </div>
 *         {% endif %}
 *     </div>
 *     
 *     <div style="margin-top: 20px; padding-top: 20px; border-top: 1px solid #dee2e6; font-size: 12px; color: #6c757d;">
 *         <p>© {{ year }} Eviction Management System. All rights reserved.</p>
 *         <p>If you have any questions, please contact us at <a href="mailto:support@evictionmanagement.com" style="color: #0d6efd;">support@evictionmanagement.com</a>.</p>
 *     </div>
 * </body>
 * </html>
 * ```
 */

// Template Naming Conventions
/**
 * Template files should follow these naming conventions:
 * - Use lowercase letters
 * - Use underscores to separate words
 * - Be descriptive but concise
 * - Use consistent prefixes for related templates
 * 
 * Examples:
 * - user_profile.html
 * - eviction_details.html
 * - property_list.html
 * - tenant_edit_form.html
 */

// JavaScript Integration
/**
 * When integrating JavaScript with templates:
 * - Include scripts at the end of the body
 * - Use data attributes to pass data to JavaScript
 * - Keep JavaScript minimal in templates
 * - Use event delegation for dynamically added elements
 * 
 * Example:
 * ```html
 * <button 
 *     class="btn btn-primary" 
 *     data-action="view-timeline" 
 *     data-eviction-id="{{ eviction.id }}"
 *     data-eviction-status="{{ eviction.status }}"
 * >
 *     View Timeline
 * </button>
 * 
 * {% block extra_js %}
 * <script>
 *     document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function() {
 *         document.querySelectorAll('[data-action="view-timeline"]').forEach(button => {
 *             button.addEventListener('click', function() {
 *                 const evictionId = this.dataset.evictionId;
 *                 const evictionStatus = this.dataset.evictionStatus;
 *                 // Handle button click
 *             });
 *         });
 *     });
 * </script>
 * {% endblock %}
 * ```
 */

// Color System
/**
 * Use consistent color variables throughout templates:
 * - primary: #0d6efd (primary actions, links)
 * - secondary: #6c757d (secondary actions)
 * - success: #198754 (success messages, completed statuses)
 * - danger: #dc3545 (errors, destructive actions)
 * - warning: #ffc107 (warnings, caution states)
 * - info: #0dcaf0 (informational messages)
 * - dark: #212529 (text, headers)
 * - light: #f8f9fa (backgrounds)
 * 
 * Status-specific colors:
 * - filed: #0dcaf0 (info)
 * - pending: #ffc107 (warning)
 * - scheduled: #6f42c1 (purple)
 * - judgment: #fd7e14 (orange)
 * - eviction: #dc3545 (danger)
 * - completed: #198754 (success)
 * - dismissed: #6c757d (secondary)
 */

// Accessibility Requirements
/**
 * All templates must adhere to these accessibility guidelines:
 * - Use semantic HTML elements
 * - Include proper ARIA attributes
 * - Maintain sufficient color contrast
 * - Ensure keyboard navigability
 * - Provide text alternatives for images
 * - Use descriptive link text
 * 
 * Example:
 * ```html
 * <!-- Bad -->
 * <div class="header">Main Navigation</div>
 * <div class="nav-item">
 *     <div class="nav-link" onclick="goToPage('dashboard')">Dashboard</div>
 * </div>
 * 
 * <!-- Good -->
 * <nav aria-label="Main Navigation">
 *     <ul class="nav">
 *         <li class="nav-item">
 *             <a class="nav-link" href="{{ url_for('dashboard') }}">Dashboard</a>
 *         </li>
 *     </ul>
 * </nav>
 * ```
 */

// Responsive Design
/**
 * Templates should follow these responsive design principles:
 * - Use Bootstrap's grid system for layouts
 * - Test on multiple device sizes
 * - Use appropriate breakpoints
 * - Optimize tables for mobile viewing
 * - Consider touch interfaces for interactive elements
 * 
 * Example:
 * ```html
 * <div class="row">
 *     <div class="col-12 col-md-6 col-lg-4">
 *         <!-- Content adapted for different screen sizes -->
 *     </div>
 * </div>
 * ```
 */ 